= Testing Strategy =

{{info}}
Updated 2026-09-23: rewritten for the current test layers. The 30-case baseline suite, the A/B prompt tests, the ##npm test:regression## suite and their cost table no longer exist. The previous version of this page is archived in ##Docs/xwiki-pages-ARCHIVE/FactHarbor/Product Development/DevOps/Guidelines/Testing Strategy/WebHome_arch.xwiki##.
{{/info}}

== Overview ==

FactHarbor's testing strategy focuses on measurement-driven quality improvement:

1. **Quality baselines**: reports are judged against Captain-defined inputs and accepted bands
1. **Before/after comparison**: validation batches compare the same inputs across two builds
1. **Regression prevention**: the default test suite runs locally and in CI
1. **Continuous validation**: analysis jobs record metrics

|= Layer |= Command |= Calls real LLM or search providers
| Default test suite | ##npm test## | No
| CI guardrail | ##npm run test:ci##, web and API builds, API tests | No
| LLM integration suites | ##test:llm##, ##test:neutrality##, ##test:cb-integration##, ##test:smoke##, ##test:expensive## | Yes
| Prompt evaluation | ##promptfoo##, ##promptfoo:sr## | Yes
| Calibration lanes | ##test:calibration:smoke##, ##test:calibration:canary##, ##test:calibration:gate## | Yes
| Validation batches | ##npm run validate:run -- <batchLabel> <familiesFile>## | Yes, submits live analysis jobs

The ##test:*## and ##promptfoo## commands in this table are the scripts in ##apps/web/package.json##; run them from ##apps/web## or with ##npm -w apps/web run <script>##. The root ##package.json## has its own ##promptfoo*## wrappers (##scripts/promptfoo-sr.js##); from the root, ##npm run promptfoo## runs the source-reliability config rather than ##promptfooconfig.yaml##. ##npm test##, ##npm run test:ci## and the ##validate:*## scripts run from the repository root.

== Default Test Suite ==

* Vitest suites live in ##apps/web/test/## (##unit/##, ##integration/##, ##calibration/##).
* ##npm test## excludes the suites that call real LLMs; the exclusion list is in ##apps/web/vitest.config.ts##.
* Some local tests can still contact running services or write local state. Check a test before running it against a live stack.
* CI (##.github/workflows/ci.yml##) runs ##npm run test:ci##, builds the web app and the API, and runs the offline API tests (##apps/api.Tests##) on pushes to ##main## and on pull requests. It makes no LLM calls.

== Real-LLM Suites ==

* ##test:llm##: LLM provider integration
* ##test:neutrality##: input neutrality; a question and the equivalent statement must yield the same analysis (target: average absolute divergence ≤ 4 percentage points)
* ##test:cb-integration##: the full ClaimAssessmentBoundary pipeline
* ##test:smoke##: the hydrogen versus electricity efficiency scenario (##apps/web/test/integration/hydrogen-smoke.test.ts##)
* ##test:expensive##: the four suites above in one run

Each of these scripts first runs ##apps/web/scripts/assert-local-live-tests.js##, which blocks it on GitHub Actions. It then runs its test files under ##apps/web/vitest.live.config.ts##, because ##apps/web/vitest.config.ts## excludes them from the default run.

== Quality Baselines ==

Report quality is judged against Captain-defined expectations:

* ##Docs/AGENTS/Captain_Quality_Expectations.md##: Captain intent and the best comparator reports
* ##Docs/AGENTS/benchmark-expectations.json##: scored benchmark inputs with accepted verdict, truth and confidence bands
* ##Docs/AGENTS/report-quality-expectations.json##: structural Q-code checks
* ##npm run validate:quality-drift##: checks that the band table in ##Captain_Quality_Expectations.md## matches ##benchmark-expectations.json##, that Q-code field paths resolve to fields in the analyzer types, and that recent ##Prompt_Issue_Register.md## entries carry a Q-code

Validation and benchmark runs must use only the analysis inputs that the Captain has defined in ##AGENTS.md## (Captain-Defined Analysis Inputs).

== Validation Batches ==

##npm run validate:run -- <batchLabel> [familiesFile]## submits each family in the families file and waits for its job, up to a per-job time limit set in the script, before submitting the next. The default file, ##scripts/validation/validation-families.json##, holds the 8 scored benchmark inputs, named like the families in ##benchmark-expectations.json##; any other families file must contain only Captain-defined inputs. The script writes a summary for each successful family to ##test-output/validation/<batchLabel>/##, and a ##manifest.json## there when the batch completes. It submits with the invite code in ##FH_INVITE_CODE##. ##npm run validate:compare -- <oldDir> <newDir>## prints a markdown comparison of two batches.

Before submitting a batch, commit the change under test and refresh the running services. If the first 3 jobs already show a clear regression, stop the batch (##AGENTS.md##, Live Job Submission Discipline).

== Calibration ==

The calibration lanes (smoke, canary, gate) measure run reliability and framing skew. Lane purpose, thresholds and the run registry are in ##Docs/STATUS/Calibration_Run_Policy.md##.

== Test Environments ==

=== Local Development ===
* SQLite database
* Default test suite without real LLM calls
* Real-LLM suites, calibration lanes and validation batches run here, each on explicit approval

=== CI/CD ===
* Default test suite and builds only (no LLM calls), on pushes to ##main## and on pull requests

== Cost Management ==

=== Cost Control ===

1. **Budget Approval Required**: every run that calls real LLM or search providers needs explicit approval for that run and its scope
1. **Cost Tracking**: estimate the cost before execution
1. **Abort on Threshold**: stop if cost exceeds the approved budget, and stop a validation batch early once a regression is clear
1. **Use Budget Models**: for non-critical test validation

== Continuous Monitoring ==

=== Production Metrics ===

Analysis jobs record metrics, including duration, token counts, estimated cost (when every LLM call can be priced), quality-gate statistics and per-call schema-compliance flags. The Analysis Monitoring dashboard (##/admin/quality-health##) aggregates them.

=== Alerts ===

Metric-threshold alerts are not implemented. An opt-in webhook (##FH_WEBHOOK_URL##) posts ##system_paused## when the runner auto-pauses after provider failures, and ##system_paused## or ##system_resumed## when an admin pauses or resumes the system; an automatic resume is not posted. Uptime monitoring and cross-job error alerting are tracked as ##OPS-MONITOR## in ##Docs/STATUS/Backlog.md## (deferred). Candidate threshold conditions:
* Schema compliance <90%
* Average cost >2x baseline
* Average duration >2x baseline
* Gate 1 pass rate <50%

== Performance Testing ==

=== Load Testing ===

Not in place yet. For production, use k6 or Artillery to test:
* Concurrent analyses
* Database query performance
* API rate limits

== Test Data ==

=== Benchmark vs Real ===

**Benchmark** (Captain-defined inputs):
* Controlled, reproducible
* Compared against accepted bands
* Enable regression detection

**Real** (production analyses):
* Uncontrolled, varied
* True user scenarios
* Enable drift detection

=== Privacy ===

Test cases must NOT include:
* Real user data
* Sensitive information
* Copyrighted material

